[1mThe Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m aborted (SIGABRT) where the C segfaults (SIGSEGV)[22m on any null-pointer input — rows E25–E27. Root cause: rustc's [38;5;10mub_checks[0m, enabled by [38;5;10mdebug-assertions[0m, inserts a null/alignment check ahead of every raw-pointer deref. That check panics, and a panic inside an [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m fn is non-unwinding, so the process aborts. C has no such check. Fixed in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m by disabling [38;5;10mdebug-assertions[0m and [38;5;10moverflow-checks[0m in [1mboth[22m profiles (the translation already models C's wrapping overflow explicitly via [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m), with a regression guard ([38;5;10mrust_so_has_no_ub_check_instrumentation[0m) that greps the built [38;5;10m.so[0m for the ub-check panic strings.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This was only reachable in the dev profile — it is exactly the class of bug that testing one configuration misses.[0m[0m
